WEBVTT

00:11.017 --> 00:12.060
‎GRADE 2 CLASS 2

00:12.144 --> 00:15.272
‎So, we've decided on
<i>‎Aladdin and the Magic Lamp</i>‎.

00:15.355 --> 00:16.690
‎PLAY
‎ALADDIN, MOMOTARO, OPERA, ALICE

00:16.773 --> 00:18.108
‎-Yay!
‎-Wow!

00:18.191 --> 00:19.943
‎All right, who wants to be in the cast?

00:20.027 --> 00:21.319
‎GRADE 2 CLASS 2
‎CLASS REPRESENTATIVES

00:21.403 --> 00:22.404
‎EXCITED

00:22.487 --> 00:23.572
‎Right here!

00:24.156 --> 00:25.574
‎Glance.

00:25.657 --> 00:27.492
‎Glancing... Glance.

00:27.576 --> 00:28.577
‎WHOA

00:30.036 --> 00:31.705
‎No, no, no!

00:32.539 --> 00:33.540
‎Tch...

00:34.291 --> 00:35.584
‎BECKON

00:40.464 --> 00:41.465
‎Swish.

00:41.548 --> 00:42.966
‎OH...
‎WHOA...

00:43.592 --> 00:45.719
<i>‎Aw, I love you.</i>

00:45.802 --> 00:48.638
‎No, not like that, though.

00:50.307 --> 00:52.976
‎Can we finish without working
‎over summer break?

00:53.643 --> 00:56.480
‎Okay, let's work out everyone's schedules.

00:58.732 --> 01:01.234
‎Love how proactive they all are.

01:01.318 --> 01:02.486
‎HOMEROOM TEACHER

01:08.325 --> 01:10.368
<i>‎This distance between Hikawa and me...</i>

01:11.078 --> 01:13.997
<i>‎Seems like we get closer,
‎then drift apart...</i>

01:14.623 --> 01:16.124
<i>‎Am I just imagining it?</i>

01:16.708 --> 01:18.877
‎Might as well go all out on the backdrop.

01:20.962 --> 01:22.756
‎WAVE WAVE

01:23.757 --> 01:24.758
‎LOOKS AWAY

01:28.261 --> 01:29.262
<i>‎If I...</i>

01:30.514 --> 01:32.474
<i>‎just gave up completely,</i>

01:33.058 --> 01:34.476
<i>‎then nothing would happen</i>

01:34.976 --> 01:37.771
<i>‎and no one would get hurt.</i>

01:38.396 --> 01:41.399
<i>‎But I can't help wanting
‎to close this distance.</i>

01:42.400 --> 01:44.277
<i>‎Is that just selfish of me?</i>

01:46.488 --> 01:48.156
‎NINE MOMOKA - CAN'T WAIT
‎FOR THE CONCERT TOMORROW!

01:48.240 --> 01:50.367
<i>‎Can't wait for the concert tomorrow!</i>

03:21.499 --> 03:25.921
‎EPISODE 16
‎STOP AND GO

03:31.426 --> 03:32.677
‎Okay.

03:37.140 --> 03:38.183
‎Amamiya--

03:39.893 --> 03:41.186
‎Nice to meet you.

03:42.520 --> 03:44.648
‎I'm Aoyagi.

03:44.731 --> 03:46.733
‎Who'd you think he was?

03:46.816 --> 03:48.526
‎We're on the soccer team together.

03:48.610 --> 03:52.155
‎They said they were going
‎to the band concert, so I tagged along.

03:52.239 --> 03:53.823
‎Nice to meet you.

03:54.658 --> 03:57.285
‎The venue's that way.

04:00.997 --> 04:02.666
‎Thank you very much!

04:02.749 --> 04:04.834
‎MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL BAND

04:04.918 --> 04:08.630
‎-Maru!
‎-What? Where did Amamiya and Hino go?

04:09.214 --> 04:13.093
‎Oh, Yota said he'd watch from the back
‎since he's tall.

04:13.176 --> 04:15.679
‎Amamiya went that way too.

04:15.762 --> 04:17.597
‎Oh, then I'll go too.

04:18.890 --> 04:20.350
‎Yeah!

04:21.184 --> 04:22.602
‎What?

04:28.275 --> 04:29.276
‎Are you okay?

04:36.074 --> 04:37.617
‎LOCAL LINES (EAST EXIT GATES)
‎SUBWAY (WEST EXIT GATES)

04:38.201 --> 04:39.828
‎Well, we're headed that way.

04:44.582 --> 04:46.459
‎Amamiya.

04:46.543 --> 04:47.627
‎What's wrong?

04:49.754 --> 04:51.881
‎No. Never mind.

04:59.347 --> 05:00.598
‎See you.

05:03.601 --> 05:04.644
‎SUBWAY

05:07.689 --> 05:12.235
‎Why don't you either lead her on
‎or push her away?

05:17.615 --> 05:21.745
<i>‎Of course I know how Kuriki feels.</i>

05:22.537 --> 05:25.832
<i>‎But,
‎I can't return her feelings right now.</i>

05:26.750 --> 05:27.792
<i>‎But still...</i>

05:28.460 --> 05:31.463
<i>‎I just don't see why it's wrong</i>

05:31.963 --> 05:33.923
<i>‎not to push someone away.</i>

05:37.135 --> 05:39.179
<i>‎Oh, man!</i>

05:41.014 --> 05:42.015
‎BREADSTICKS

05:44.392 --> 05:45.769
‎Oh, you're awake.

05:49.147 --> 05:50.815
‎Wait, you're eating something.

05:52.317 --> 05:53.651
‎Feeling down?

05:53.735 --> 05:55.070
‎Want some bread too?

05:55.153 --> 05:57.822
‎Wait, Koyun brought this?

05:59.574 --> 06:00.784
‎Here.

06:00.867 --> 06:01.868
‎Thanks.

06:02.535 --> 06:04.537
‎MUNCH MUNCH MUNCH MUNCH

06:05.538 --> 06:06.790
‎SO PEACEFUL...

06:06.873 --> 06:08.958
<i>‎Wait, what's going on here?</i>

06:13.213 --> 06:14.214
‎GRIN

06:14.297 --> 06:15.465
‎THUD

06:16.800 --> 06:17.801
‎WHOA

06:24.933 --> 06:25.975
‎SPRING UP

06:29.938 --> 06:32.232
<i>‎What? That just now...</i>

06:33.024 --> 06:35.235
<i>‎What was that? That was so cute.</i>

06:35.318 --> 06:36.361
‎I told you!

06:36.444 --> 06:37.445
‎BONK BONK BONK

06:37.529 --> 06:38.863
‎I'm fine being friends.

06:39.948 --> 06:42.325
‎All the more reason if you're friends.

06:42.951 --> 06:44.452
‎You should be able to

06:45.036 --> 06:46.788
‎talk normally when you're together.

06:50.667 --> 06:55.255
<i>‎I'd started wondering
‎how I should act around him.</i>

06:57.132 --> 06:58.591
‎But I realized we're friends,

06:59.134 --> 07:01.094
‎and things are just the same as before.

07:02.428 --> 07:04.931
‎I feel a lot clearer now.

07:05.014 --> 07:06.015
‎You do?

07:06.808 --> 07:08.560
‎Wanna go back to class?

07:08.643 --> 07:10.520
‎If you drop that weird face.

07:10.603 --> 07:13.022
‎HUP HUP

07:14.232 --> 07:15.066
‎SNAP

07:20.029 --> 07:21.030
‎GRIN

07:21.698 --> 07:22.907
‎HEH

07:22.991 --> 07:24.284
<i>‎What's with that face?</i>

07:26.286 --> 07:27.287
‎GRIN

07:27.370 --> 07:29.539
‎HEH - HEH

07:30.248 --> 07:31.249
‎Later.

07:36.671 --> 07:37.797
<i>‎What was that?</i>

07:37.881 --> 07:41.593
<i>‎I thought she'd been avoiding me lately.</i>

07:42.343 --> 07:43.928
<i>‎Wait...</i>

07:44.012 --> 07:45.346
<i>‎I'll get the wrong idea.</i>

07:46.139 --> 07:49.434
<i>‎No, no, no. That's not it.</i>

07:49.976 --> 07:53.480
<i>‎I'm not going to resent her
‎for not feeling the same.</i>

07:54.022 --> 07:56.024
<i>‎These feelings are one-sided.</i>

07:56.107 --> 07:59.152
<i>‎They're mine and mine alone.</i>

07:59.903 --> 08:01.446
‎WICKED WIZARD - AMAMIYA

08:01.529 --> 08:02.947
‎I'm the villain?

08:04.824 --> 08:05.825
<i>‎So...</i>

08:07.785 --> 08:08.828
‎It'd suit you.

08:09.829 --> 08:10.830
‎Hey...

08:11.706 --> 08:13.374
‎What's that supposed to mean?

08:13.458 --> 08:14.459
‎LOOKS AWAY

08:14.542 --> 08:16.085
<i>‎Wow...</i>

08:16.169 --> 08:18.213
<i>‎She looks so happy.</i>

08:19.631 --> 08:21.466
<i>‎So, just a little longer...</i>

08:23.426 --> 08:24.719
‎Koyun.

08:26.262 --> 08:27.430
‎Hey.

08:27.514 --> 08:29.224
<i>‎Let me see how you really feel.</i>

08:30.016 --> 08:33.228
‎Wanna go somewhere over summer break?

08:35.855 --> 08:39.776
<i>‎If I don't have a chance,
‎I'll back off for good.</i>

08:42.195 --> 08:43.530
‎Well...

08:43.613 --> 08:44.614
‎Yeah.

08:44.697 --> 08:46.032
‎Sure.

08:46.115 --> 08:47.242
‎That sounds good.

08:48.826 --> 08:52.622
‎We should all go somewhere again.

08:56.042 --> 08:57.126
‎Yeah.

08:57.210 --> 08:59.045
‎We'll figure out a day.

08:59.671 --> 09:00.713
‎All of us.

09:02.298 --> 09:03.299
‎Yeah.

09:03.800 --> 09:04.801
‎Later.

09:13.101 --> 09:15.478
<i>‎That was close. Too close.</i>

09:16.437 --> 09:18.731
<i>‎I almost got the wrong idea again.</i>

09:19.774 --> 09:23.820
<i>‎For a second,
‎I thought he meant just the two of us.</i>

09:25.655 --> 09:26.698
<i>‎No.</i>

09:26.781 --> 09:28.116
<i>‎I can't get my hopes up.</i>

09:28.950 --> 09:33.079
<i>‎I don't want to get my hopes up,
‎get excited, then end up disappointed.</i>

09:33.705 --> 09:35.707
<i>‎Get over it. Move on.</i>

09:39.836 --> 09:41.129
‎Oh, Koyun.

09:41.879 --> 09:43.256
‎Momoka.

09:51.556 --> 09:55.268
‎Oh, I went to a concert
‎with Amamiya the other day.

09:55.351 --> 09:56.394
‎TWITCH

09:56.477 --> 10:00.940
<i>‎When the crowd suddenly rushed in,
‎he helped me out.</i>

10:01.024 --> 10:03.067
<i>‎He was so cool.</i>

10:04.235 --> 10:06.237
‎It totally made my heart skip a beat.

10:06.904 --> 10:07.905
‎I see.

10:09.741 --> 10:14.704
‎I'm thinking of asking him
‎to hang out again over summer break.

10:14.787 --> 10:15.913
‎What do you think?

10:17.498 --> 10:21.127
<i>‎Why would she choose me
‎to talk about this?</i>

10:21.878 --> 10:26.424
<i>‎In the first place, why did she suddenly
‎start getting close to me?</i>

10:27.133 --> 10:28.384
<i>‎What's in it for her?</i>

10:28.468 --> 10:29.677
<i>‎A buffer?</i>

10:30.428 --> 10:31.429
<i>‎A go-between?</i>

10:32.472 --> 10:35.058
<i>‎She's my friend. So I love her.</i>

10:35.725 --> 10:39.979
<i>‎To Amamiya, I'm not really anyone special.</i>

10:40.855 --> 10:43.858
<i>‎But, the same goes for her.</i>

10:44.692 --> 10:46.861
‎I have no right to decide that for him.

10:50.406 --> 10:52.617
<i>‎I should just leave it alone.</i>

10:53.910 --> 10:55.536
<i>‎If I keep getting involved,</i>

10:56.204 --> 10:58.998
<i>‎I'll just face the part of me
‎I hate again.</i>

10:59.540 --> 11:01.042
<i>‎What a pain.</i>

11:03.544 --> 11:05.380
‎Well, I'm going the other way, so...

11:07.799 --> 11:08.800
‎See you.

11:11.260 --> 11:14.305
<i>‎How can she be so positive
‎and just go for it like that?</i>

11:15.723 --> 11:16.724
<i>‎I don't care.</i>

11:17.308 --> 11:18.893
<i>‎I don't, I don't.</i>

11:18.976 --> 11:21.062
<i>‎My heart isn't that pure.</i>

11:21.646 --> 11:24.482
<i>‎"You'll only get hurt,
‎so you should give up."</i>

11:25.316 --> 11:26.484
<i>‎But I won't tell her that.</i>

11:28.236 --> 11:31.489
<i>‎Momoka, is it true you're dating him?</i>

11:32.240 --> 11:36.536
<i>‎Why? You knew
‎I loved him first, didn't you?</i>

11:36.619 --> 11:39.705
<i>‎So what? Does liking him first
‎make you better?</i>

11:39.789 --> 11:41.624
<i>‎He's the one who came on strong.</i>

11:44.710 --> 11:47.505
<i>‎Don't go after someone else's guy!</i>

11:47.588 --> 11:51.259
<i>‎If you hadn't come along,
‎we'd still be into each other.</i>

11:52.009 --> 11:54.762
<i>‎Way too calculating and two-faced.</i>

11:55.346 --> 11:56.347
<i>‎Shut up.</i>

11:57.098 --> 11:59.517
<i>‎I don't care.</i>

12:00.351 --> 12:03.229
<i>‎I was up-front
‎about my feelings this time.</i>

12:03.855 --> 12:06.482
<i>‎So don't blame me later.</i>

12:06.566 --> 12:09.735
<i>‎Even if she hates me,
‎I'm not pure-hearted anyway.</i>

12:11.028 --> 12:12.238
<i>‎I won't apologize for it.</i>

12:13.114 --> 12:15.199
<i>‎Not even for a second.</i>

12:19.162 --> 12:21.873
‎About what I told you
‎at the sports festival,

12:21.956 --> 12:24.167
‎please forget I ever said that.

12:24.250 --> 12:26.127
‎What? Why?

12:27.295 --> 12:29.630
‎Because I want us
‎to stay friends after all.

12:30.339 --> 12:32.633
‎I want to get rid of these feelings.

12:33.259 --> 12:34.635
‎These feelings?

12:35.344 --> 12:39.182
<i>‎I don't have the courage
‎to end things properly like you did, Yota.</i>

12:40.725 --> 12:45.062
‎No, mine just got found out,
‎so I had to put an end to it.

12:45.646 --> 12:48.733
‎I never planned to do anything
‎about it either,

12:48.816 --> 12:50.443
‎so I get how you feel, Koyun.

12:51.277 --> 12:52.278
‎Thanks.

12:52.862 --> 12:54.071
‎It is what it is.

12:54.155 --> 12:56.115
‎Oh, right.

12:56.199 --> 13:01.078
‎Amamiya and I talked about all of us
‎hanging out again this summer break.

13:01.162 --> 13:02.538
‎PREPARING
‎FOR THE CULTURAL FESTIVAL

13:02.622 --> 13:03.831
‎Are you...

13:03.915 --> 13:05.166
‎Well...

13:05.249 --> 13:06.501
‎Are you okay with that?

13:06.584 --> 13:08.836
‎Oh, yeah. I'm fine.

13:09.462 --> 13:12.757
‎I'm the one who got it off my chest,
‎so I feel better.

13:13.257 --> 13:15.927
‎I think Miki's probably the one
‎having a harder time.

13:16.010 --> 13:17.929
<i>‎Like what you said before...</i>

13:18.012 --> 13:19.013
‎WHAT? - I LOVE YOU
‎DIFFERENT TYPE

13:19.096 --> 13:20.556
<i>‎...love comes in all shapes and sizes.</i>

13:20.640 --> 13:21.682
‎LIKE - LOVE
‎DIFFERENT SIZE

13:22.433 --> 13:25.186
‎Being on the receiving end is hard.

13:25.269 --> 13:26.354
‎I bet.

13:29.273 --> 13:30.399
‎MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

13:30.483 --> 13:34.320
‎So then he goes all the way
‎behind the school just to get some water.

13:34.403 --> 13:35.404
‎Seriously?

13:38.616 --> 13:39.909
<i>‎"Can you meet me now?"</i>

13:39.992 --> 13:41.202
‎NINE MOMOKA
‎CAN YOU MEET ME NOW?

13:50.169 --> 13:51.254
‎What's wrong?

13:52.588 --> 13:55.466
‎Sorry for asking you out here so suddenly.

13:59.929 --> 14:06.102
‎I thought I'd wait for a better time
‎when it was convenient for you.

14:06.811 --> 14:11.274
‎But I felt like that moment
‎would never come if I just kept waiting.

14:11.816 --> 14:14.694
‎I couldn't wait any longer.

14:17.697 --> 14:20.199
‎I love you, Amamiya.

14:20.700 --> 14:21.951
‎Would you

14:22.994 --> 14:24.161
‎be my boyfriend?

14:30.293 --> 14:31.294
‎Sorry.

14:31.919 --> 14:33.462
‎It means a lot to me, but...

14:38.259 --> 14:39.927
‎SUMMER BREAK

14:44.515 --> 14:45.933
‎Tsukiko.

14:46.017 --> 14:49.103
‎We got some props that looked useful.

14:49.186 --> 14:50.438
‎Thank you.

14:50.521 --> 14:51.856
‎I'll leave these here.

14:52.523 --> 14:54.275
‎Thank you too, Yota.

14:54.358 --> 14:55.943
‎Sorry for making you help.

14:56.903 --> 14:59.697
‎Well, I'm the carpet, so no lines for me.

14:59.780 --> 15:03.367
‎Genie! Turn me into
‎the world's greatest wizard!

15:04.035 --> 15:05.202
‎EEK...

15:05.286 --> 15:07.455
‎Oh, the genie's being threatened.

15:08.164 --> 15:09.790
‎Oh, good! Great!

15:09.874 --> 15:10.958
‎CAST PRACTICING

15:11.042 --> 15:12.627
‎The villain's really leveling up.

15:12.710 --> 15:13.711
‎STARE

15:14.921 --> 15:16.380
‎Hey!

15:17.048 --> 15:19.216
‎The carpet has to join in now.

15:19.300 --> 15:22.470
‎Okay, villain. Get sucked into the lamp.

15:22.553 --> 15:24.472
‎LAMP (TEMPORARY)

15:25.097 --> 15:28.142
‎And Aladdin and the princess
‎end up together. Happy ending!

15:29.685 --> 15:31.938
‎Yota, what's with that pose?

15:32.021 --> 15:34.607
‎I'm picturing how I'll look
‎in the carpet costume.

15:37.151 --> 15:38.319
‎That'd be intimidating!

15:38.402 --> 15:40.154
‎Maybe I should at least clap.

15:44.367 --> 15:46.786
‎Wait.
‎Miki, did you change your hair color?

15:46.869 --> 15:48.120
‎You only just noticed?

15:48.204 --> 15:49.497
‎Sorry.

15:50.122 --> 15:54.001
‎Well, I can pull off
‎pretty much any color.

15:54.585 --> 15:56.504
‎Anything looks good on you, Miki.

16:01.384 --> 16:02.468
‎Yeah!

16:02.551 --> 16:04.011
<i>‎I was just kidding though...</i>

16:07.598 --> 16:08.724
‎Amamiya.

16:08.808 --> 16:10.893
‎You really went all in.

16:10.977 --> 16:12.103
‎I mean...

16:12.186 --> 16:14.772
‎it's hard to watch someone
‎act all embarrassed.

16:15.856 --> 16:17.024
‎Good luck.

16:18.192 --> 16:19.777
‎How are the sets coming along?

16:19.860 --> 16:22.905
‎Tsukiko's sketching them out now.

16:22.989 --> 16:24.031
‎Oh, hi.

16:24.115 --> 16:27.159
‎Other than that,
‎we're still collecting materials.

16:28.035 --> 16:29.120
‎I see.

16:29.870 --> 16:34.542
<i>‎Somehow, Amamiya and Koyuki
‎seem totally normal now.</i>

16:35.292 --> 16:37.169
<i>‎So natural it's almost unnatural...</i>

16:38.045 --> 16:42.049
<i>‎At the sports festival, they were
‎both awkward in the opposite way.</i>

16:44.885 --> 16:46.470
<i>‎These two...</i>

16:46.554 --> 16:47.805
<i>‎Did something happen?</i>

16:48.973 --> 16:50.850
<i>‎Yeah. I'm okay.</i>

16:50.933 --> 16:53.060
<i>‎I can talk to him normally now.</i>

16:53.144 --> 16:56.022
<i>‎I think the way things are now
‎is just right.</i>

16:57.857 --> 17:01.527
<i>‎I've always run away
‎from getting close to people.</i>

17:02.695 --> 17:05.281
<i>‎But slowly, my world
‎feels like it's opening up.</i>

17:06.073 --> 17:07.491
<i>‎Now I enjoy this class</i>

17:08.117 --> 17:10.661
<i>‎and school too.</i>

17:11.579 --> 17:15.791
<i>‎So the way things are now
‎feels comfortable,</i>

17:15.875 --> 17:16.876
<i>‎just right.</i>

17:17.626 --> 17:19.295
<i>‎Yeah, that's it.</i>

17:19.920 --> 17:21.255
<i>‎I'm sure that's it.</i>

17:24.341 --> 17:26.677
‎Okay, that's enough for today.

17:26.761 --> 17:28.387
‎-Nice work!
‎-Well done!

17:28.471 --> 17:29.805
‎Oh, Koyun.

17:31.515 --> 17:32.516
‎Hello.

17:33.100 --> 17:35.144
‎Momoka, what's up?

17:37.813 --> 17:39.774
‎Where did Minato go?

17:41.734 --> 17:42.902
<i>‎"Minato"?</i>

17:44.236 --> 17:47.031
‎We were supposed to go home together.

17:47.865 --> 17:48.866
‎What?

17:50.201 --> 17:51.202
‎What...

17:51.285 --> 17:52.787
‎Minato didn't tell you?

17:54.080 --> 17:56.123
‎We're dating.

17:57.917 --> 17:58.918
‎What?

18:01.712 --> 18:02.755
‎Would you

18:03.631 --> 18:05.299
‎be my boyfriend?

18:09.386 --> 18:10.471
‎Sorry.

18:10.554 --> 18:12.056
‎It means a lot to me, but...

18:12.139 --> 18:16.060
‎Because you love someone else,
‎you can't go out with me?

18:17.269 --> 18:20.106
‎I can tell just by watching you

18:20.731 --> 18:23.526
‎that there's someone you love.

18:24.151 --> 18:27.571
‎You say my feelings
‎mean a lot to you, but...

18:28.114 --> 18:31.325
‎I know you don't see me that way at all.

18:32.076 --> 18:33.911
‎I know all that.

18:37.248 --> 18:39.792
‎Does the girl you love

18:40.417 --> 18:42.294
‎feel the same way about you?

18:42.920 --> 18:44.839
‎Even if you love someone else,

18:45.548 --> 18:47.424
‎I can't give up.

18:48.884 --> 18:50.886
‎You really hit me where it hurts.

18:51.720 --> 18:53.097
‎Doesn't it hurt?

18:54.640 --> 18:56.433
‎You think it doesn't?

18:56.517 --> 18:59.854
‎Then why not choose me?

19:02.231 --> 19:03.399
‎You know,

19:03.482 --> 19:06.235
‎I'm not as good a guy as you think I am.

19:07.027 --> 19:10.656
‎I've dated people
‎just because they asked me to.

19:11.365 --> 19:13.450
‎And I hurt a lot of people.

19:14.118 --> 19:17.621
‎I don't think I should do that anymore.

19:18.330 --> 19:22.459
‎So that's why you can't be my boyfriend?

19:23.752 --> 19:24.753
‎Yeah.

19:35.014 --> 19:36.223
‎You say

19:36.724 --> 19:38.726
‎you're not a good person,

19:38.809 --> 19:41.353
‎that you've hurt your ex-girlfriends.

19:41.437 --> 19:43.230
‎But none of that

19:43.814 --> 19:47.234
‎has anything to do with me, does it?

19:47.318 --> 19:48.485
‎What?

19:48.569 --> 19:51.488
‎I'm not even part of that equation.

19:51.572 --> 19:57.745
‎What you don't like about me,
‎how you feel about me...

19:58.245 --> 20:01.707
‎Anything you actually think
‎or feel about me,

20:02.374 --> 20:04.168
‎none of that even comes into it,

20:04.251 --> 20:05.878
‎because you don't see me at all.

20:06.712 --> 20:08.923
‎That's just too sad.

20:10.424 --> 20:13.219
‎I'm not even at the starting line.

20:13.302 --> 20:16.096
‎I don't want to give up

20:16.180 --> 20:17.514
‎on these feelings yet.

20:22.311 --> 20:23.562
‎I love you.

20:24.188 --> 20:26.941
‎Please give me a chance.

20:34.406 --> 20:37.076
‎Don't cry, Kuriki.

20:38.452 --> 20:39.578
‎Let's give it a try.

20:43.916 --> 20:45.501
‎What?

20:46.877 --> 20:48.587
‎-You mean it?
‎-Yeah.

20:48.671 --> 20:50.589
‎Wow... Yay!

20:51.257 --> 20:53.509
‎-"Yay"?
‎-Wow, no way!

20:54.176 --> 20:57.554
‎Amamiya,
‎you actually carry a handkerchief, huh?

20:57.638 --> 20:59.306
‎Handy at times like this, right?

20:59.390 --> 21:01.058
‎Wow, that's so cheesy.

21:04.520 --> 21:06.897
‎So, we're together now.

21:06.981 --> 21:08.107
‎The two of us.

21:10.192 --> 21:16.782
<i>‎Honestly, I never thought I'd say that
‎in such a clumsy, desperate way.</i>

21:17.574 --> 21:19.451
<i>‎But I'm the one dating him now.</i>

21:20.202 --> 21:22.121
‎Since when?

21:22.204 --> 21:24.581
‎A little before summer break started.

21:25.082 --> 21:30.629
<i>‎Part of me does wonder
‎if Minato's hiding that we're dating.</i>

21:31.547 --> 21:36.218
<i>‎Every time I saw her,
‎I couldn't stop feeling uneasy.</i>

21:37.011 --> 21:39.138
<i>‎But once she wasn't an obstacle,</i>

21:39.221 --> 21:40.222
<i>‎I couldn't care less</i>

21:41.015 --> 21:42.141
<i>‎about her now.</i>

21:44.226 --> 21:47.521
‎Well, Koyun, I'm going to go find Minato.

21:48.939 --> 21:49.940
‎Bye.

21:54.194 --> 21:56.280
‎MEITEN HIGH SCHOOL

21:56.363 --> 21:57.740
‎What?

22:00.159 --> 22:01.994
‎Isn't that Minato and Kuriki?

22:05.622 --> 22:06.623
‎Hey, quiet!

22:07.374 --> 22:09.543
‎Wait, are those two dating?

22:09.626 --> 22:10.627
‎Looks like it.

22:15.341 --> 22:18.427
‎Koyun,
‎sorry we left you to clean up alone.

22:18.510 --> 22:19.511
‎Sorry.

22:21.138 --> 22:22.264
‎Koyun?

23:50.936 --> 23:55.941
‎Subtitle translation by: Ryoko Quirke
